<!--
  IL2CPP managed-code stripping preservation for the RTMPE SDK runtime.

  The SDK locates [RtmpeRpc] handlers and [NetworkVariable] members by
  reflection and invokes them through MethodInfo.Invoke. The stripper cannot
  prove those members are reachable from a static call site, so on an AOT
  (iOS / IL2CPP) build it would remove them and the corresponding RPCs and
  replicated variables would silently stop firing on device. Preserving the
  runtime assembly keeps that reflective surface intact.

  Game-side [RtmpeRpc] methods, custom NetworkVariable<T> closed types, and
  [RtmpeRpcSerializable] payload types live in the consumer's own assembly and
  must be preserved there as well — see Documentation~/troubleshooting.md
  ("IL2CPP").

  ⚠️ The payload types are the ones with a failure mode of their own. Each is
  built through the public parameterless constructor RpcTypeRegistry resolves at
  registration; no static call site reaches that constructor, so the stripper
  may remove it while leaving the type. The type then resolves by name and can
  never be instantiated, and every RPC carrying it surfaces that parameter as
  null — one startup warning, and silence thereafter.
-->
<linker>
    <assembly fullname="RTMPE.SDK.Runtime" preserve="all" />
</linker>
